title: "DRMYN Studio: Metadata-Only Element-First AI Film Production Pipeline with SC0001 Selected Take and Readiness-Gated Omni 3 Dialogue Rendering"
type: software
version: 0.16.2-native-audio-dialogue-rendering
date-released: 2026-05-16
repository-code: "https://github.com/hknbb/drmyn-studio-public"
url: "https://github.com/hknbb/drmyn-studio-public/releases/tag/v0.16.2-native-audio-dialogue-rendering"
abstract: >
  DRMYN Studio is a metadata-only, schema-validated, human-gated research
  software framework for AI-assisted movie development and movie production
  process design, documentation, validation, and reproducibility. This
  checkpoint (v0.16.2) completes the element-first SC0001 production baseline
  and introduces readiness-gated Omni 3 native-audio dialogue rendering: a
  three-PR patch (guidance refresh, adapter implementation, suppressed-path
  proof) that embeds verified @alias-keyed dialogue into Kling Omni prompt_text
  when all speakers are native_audio_readiness: ready, or emits an exact
  suppression note when blocked. SC0001 SH001 TAKE002 was selected as canon
  (QC score 88/100). The repository provides canonical source records, planning
  metadata, prompt governance, JSON schema validation (55+ schemas, draft
  2020-12), human approval workflows, evidence records, and reproducibility
  infrastructure for AI-assisted film production. Generated media outputs are
  stored externally and referenced through metadata-only records. Demonstrated
  through the Closing Price AI-assisted film project.
